                    db_allheld: "No turning point against you: all four rounds held, so the room discounted nothing it granted.",
                    db_task: "Round 1 — fixing the slides, not the self. You read the interruption as a roadmap-quality problem. A rebuilt roadmap does not, on its own, move a 38% pulse survey: the room's doubt was not about the slides.",
                    db_misread: "Round 1 — you read the interruption as politics or as a test of technical competence. Both are plausible, and neither names what the CEO's line put in question: whether she is yet a leader.",
                    db_first: "Round 1 — the first move argued, explained away or went quiet. To a room that already has doubts, each of those reads as confirmation of them.",
                    db_solo: "Round 2 — Roche opened up to no one. Handling it herself looked strong, and left her with nobody to test her decisions against.",
